<title>POLAND: POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES FLAT AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES FLAT AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills held flat at today's primary auction on total demand of 609 million zlotys against a 400 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold 400 million zlotys worth of bills.  </p>
<p>The ministry also said that next Monday it will offer 1.3</p>
<p>billion zlotys worth of T-bills, in line with earlier plans.</p>
<p>    T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---	---     90.03     ---     81.85</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---	---    (90.03)    ---    (81.85)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---	---     90.07     ---     81.90</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---	---    (90.10)    ---    (82.07)</p>
<p>   offer		---	---     100.0     ---     300.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---	---     163.6     ---     445.1</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---	---     100.0     ---     100.0</p>
<p>   next auction    200.0    300.0    200.0     ---     600.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
